   "Status [ref]": "https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/region-del-bio-bio/2023/10/25/tras-9-anos-comite-de-ministros-aprueba-cuestionado-proyecto-terminal-maritimo-gnl-penco-lirquen.shtml, https://www.terram.cl/sorpresa-en-el-biobio-comite-de-ministros-aprobo-resistido-proyecto-gnl-penco-lirquen/",
   "Country/Area": "Chile",
   "Researcher": "Gregor Clark",
   "LastUpdated": "2026-08-04",
   "ResearcherNotesUnit": "GC, Aug 2026: Environmental approval (RCA) for this project was reaffirmed in Feb 2026...\nhttps://www.diarioconcepcion.cl/politica/2026/02/23/comite-de-ministros-ratifica-rca-favorable-para-terminal-gnl-penco-lirquen.html\n...but its fate remained uncertain as of Mar 2026, with two cases opposing the project still being litigated before the Third Environmental Court, led by the NGO Environmental Defense on behalf of the community of Penco.\nhttps://www.ongdefensaambiental.cl/comite-de-ministros-rechaza-solicitud-de-invalidacion-en-caso-gnl-penco-lirquen-pero-el-proceso-se-mantiene-en-curso-ante-el-tercer-tribunal-ambiental/\nRR, Aug 2025: Per Amalia's comments, consider shelving in '26 cycle if sponsor does not appear to be pursuing the project. See https://www.alpesenergy.com/blog/2025/08/29/chile-como-es-la-infraestructura-de-abastecimiento-de-gas-natural/ \nAL, Aug 2025: \"Pese a ser mencionado dentro del programa, desde la compañía GM Energy no confirmaron la ejecución del proyecto en el corto plazo y señalaron que actualmente el foco de la compañía está en concretar proyectos de energías renovables, principalmente solar y de almacenamiento, que apoyen la meta país de carbono neutralidad a 2050.\"https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/region-del-bio-bio/2024/09/26/gobierno-prioriza-proyecto-gnl-penco-lirquen-pero-compania-no-confirma-su-ejecucion-en-corto-plazo.shtml\nGC, Sep 2024: Project received long-delayed environmental approval in October 2023 and is now scheduled for commissioning in 2027, despite strong ongoing community opposition. Gregor, July 2023: Appears to be definitively scuttled, given the lack of recent news. Move to cancelled in 2024 if no further developments?",
   "ResearcherNotesProject": "Gregor, Aug 2026: Project indefinitely delayed by litigation; 2027 start date (announced in 2024) certain to be pushed back, if project even moves forward.\n\n Original owners were Biobio Genera SpA and Cheniere Energy Inc. \nhttps://www.lngindustry.com/liquefaction/31072015/cheniere-enters-lng-spa-with-central-el-campesino-1087/\n\nCurrent immediate owner is GM Energy, which is a joint venture of EDF Chile SpA and Biobío Genera SpA:\nhttps://www.portalchile.org/diario-oficial/2026/03/04/gm-energy-spa-76-240-099-5-2778219\nhttps://dequienes.cl/diario-oficial/2025/08/27/gm-developments-spa-77406644-6-2691754",
